// ===== San Francisco International Airport: the terminal complex (site 'sfoairport') =====
// Rebuilt on the real OSM footprints, local metres round 37.6160 N, -122.3870 E (+x east, +z south, y absolute):
//   International Terminal (SOM 2000): the main hall under the gull-wing roof (five lines of double-cantilevered steel
//     trusses on 20 columns, 250 m long, 'football' centre trusses, skylights over the top chords, the glass hall), the
//     podium over the roadway, the AirTrain stations in its north and south wings, Boarding Areas A and G (vaulted roofs);
//   Harvey Milk Terminal 1 (hall + the new Boarding Area B with its clerestory spine and solar roof, Boarding Area C),
//   Terminal 2 (Boarding Area D), Terminal 3 (Boarding Areas E and F), the post-security connectors;
//   the 2016 air traffic control tower (the 67 m 'torch': twisted silver cone, backlit glass slot, offset cab) and its
//     FAA base building between T1 and T2;
//   the Domestic Garage (6 levels round its light well, stair / lift towers), Garages A and G, the AirTrain stations
//     (T1, T2, T3 on the domestic garage), the BART / AirTrain station by Garage G, the curbside canopies;
//   jet bridges retracted beside their gates (the stands are left clear), stand markings, apron floodlight masts.
// The AirTrain guideway itself is the app's people-mover line (keepRoads 16). Its OSM 'layer 5' gives it a 33 m deck in the
// data; the real guideway runs ~10.5 m up (the station platforms are 11 m above the road): AIRTRAIN_FIX lowers the SFO
// AirTrain lines (class 16 within ~2.6 km) to 10.5 m round the terminals, ramping back up to the data height beyond
// (it edits SGR.lines[*].E before the road tiles are built; set it false to leave the data alone).
//
// window.SFO_STANDS  — the aircraft stands (for the aircraft module), WORLD metres (x east, y north = sgXY frame):
//   [{x, y, a, code, bridges, gate}, ...]  (x, y) = where the NOSE of the parked aircraft stops (on the stand centre line);
//   a = nose heading (radians, math convention: 0 = east, PI/2 = north): nose-in, pointing at the terminal facade;
//   code 'C' (A320 / 737, span <= 36 m), 'E' (777 / 787 / A350 / A330, <= 65 m), 'F' (A380 / 747-8, <= 80 m);
//   bridges = jet bridges serving the stand (door L1 5 m (C) / 7 m (E) / 9 m (F) aft of the nose, on the aircraft's left;
//   the bridges are drawn retracted: their cabs wait ~3.5 m outboard of the doors). Same format as Changi's SG_STANDS.
//   The same list is in bay/sfo/stands.json as [x, y, heading] triples.
// window.SFOAir.debugPlanes(true) draws plain aircraft silhouettes at every stand (testing only; off by default).
